# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the fuzz targets; the fuzz workflow passes
# this file in LSAN_OPTIONS. Every other leak still fails the run.
#
# iced-x86 1.21.0 builds its decoder tables once per process, in the
# lazy_static TABLES (src/decoder/handlers/tables.rs), and allocates each
# handler with Box::into_raw so the tables hold &'static references that are
# never freed. read_vex (src/decoder/table_de/mod.rs) deserializes the VEX
# map0 table as well but returns it only with iced's mvex feature, which
# borer does not enable, so once its deserializer drops, the handlers only
# map0 points at are referenced by nothing. Fuzz run 42682336514 (analyze,
# seed 3450009731) reported them at exit, 552 bytes in 12 allocations, and
# run 42703831666 symbolized that report on the same build (BuildId
# 38062a217ec2f3d7ce93cfa1128964ab4453d331): every allocation is under
# read_vex. The tables are built once, so the leak cannot grow with inputs.
leak:read_vex
